# Two opt-in prompt switches, off by default, on top of 0124. Neither changes a bit of any reply (four Sparks cabled as
# a ring, 2026-10-21: five solo greedy prompts of 5K-13K tokens, identical replies with and without).
#
# TF_GLM_DRAFT_SKIP=1: a prompt's DFlash2 taps go into the drafter's context only within reach of where it is read
#   (dflash2_multi.WindowTaps, multi._prompt_ctx): DFlash2's context is a 2,176-row ring read by 2,048-token sliding
#   windows, so only the rows within the ring's reach before the prompt's end and its kept points are committed
#   (ranges start on a full commit's 128-row steps, so those rows get the same launches); the context's end still
#   moves over every row. The rest were 128-row graph replays the host waited on at every chunk's end. +1.5-2 %
#   prompt (client time to first content, 8K-64K).
# TF_GLM_PARTIAL16=1: with bf16 partials sent p2p past two ranks (TF_GLM_PROMPT_PARTIALS=bf16, the overlap), the
#   attention output projections and the MoE combine write the peers' rows straight into the bf16 send staging and
#   this rank's into its slot of each received block (hcsplit.HcSplit.direct16; the fills take an ``out``). The e4m3
#   projections' result is bf16 already, so its fp32 widening and the side stream's conversions go; the combine's
#   fp32 sums are rounded as copy_ rounds them. +5 % prompt.
#
# Provenance and credit:
# - TF_GLM_DRAFT_SKIP follows TensorFold's window-trimmed drafter taps elsewhere (families/deepseek_v4/runtime.py: "only
#   the last window's worth is read; the rest moves the offset"; drafters/dflash_proposer.py; families/qwen3_5/
#   dflash_head.py), applied to GLM's DFlash2 ring with its kept points and 128-row commit steps.
# - TF_GLM_PARTIAL16 builds on patch 0106's bf16 partials and their send staging; the fills writing straight into that
#   staging are ours.

